    "notes": [
      "DEATH DATE/PLACE LIKELY WRONG (research 2026-07-03): multiple compiled sources (WikiTree Biggs-87; FamilySearch L6JK-22J) place this Richard Biggs's death \"probably about March 1626\" (not 1 Sept 1626 as the export has it) at West and Shirley Hundred, Charles City, Virginia (not Jamestown), and give his birth as ca. 1584, not 1590. He served in the House of Burgesses 1625-26 and left a will naming wife \"Sara\" (no surname given) and son Richard.",
      "FOUR LISTED WIVES LIKELY A MERGED-TREE ARTIFACT: the export's four spouses (Dorothy Scarlett, Sarah Anne Juxon Marshe Biggs, Sarah Browne, Agnes Henley), with marriage dates spanning 1605-1619, all predate his documented ca.-1618 Virginia marriage to \"Sarah Unknown\" — looks like several unrelated Biggs/Henley lineage guesses stacked onto one profile from other compiled trees. Treat all four as unconfirmed/legend pending a primary Hampshire parish register or Virginia land/probate record for any of them."
    ]
